Rule 261 (If the tensor dimension is greater than 0, and the max value is smaller than zero, then its data type should be complex)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ max(v_1) < 0 then (dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10)
>>
Rule 262 (if the maximum of the tensor is less than or equal to 0 and string operation is `tanh`, the tensor must be of a float data type.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if max(v_1) ≤ 0 ∧ v_2 = "tanh" then (dtype_(v_1) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 8)
>>
Rule 263 (if the shape[0] dimension is smaller than 10, and tensor is 2D, the string must not be chosen to be "ii->i" or "i,j->ij")
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if shape(v_1, 0) < 10 ∧ ndim(v_1) = 2 then v_2 ≠ "ii->i" ∧ v_2 ≠ "i,j->ij"
>>
