>>
Rule 486 (If tensor v_1 has exactly 2 dimensions and boolean v_2 is true, then the first dimension must be smaller or equal to the second dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ v_2 then shape(v_1, 0) ≤ shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 487 (If integer v_1 is smaller than 0, then v_2 must be true, else tensor v_3 must be zero dimension)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : bool, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 < 0 then v_2 else ndim(v_3) = 0
>>
Rule 488 (If float v_1 is in range [0,1], then the maximum value of tensor v_2 must be smaller or equal than 100 times shape of tensor v_2 at last dimension)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then max(v_2) ≤ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) -1) * 100
>>
Rule 489 (If bool v_1 is true, and tensor v_2's dimension is positive, then its shape at dimension 0 is different from its shape at last dimension)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 then if ndim(v_2) > 0 then shape(v_2, 0) ≠ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1)
>>
Rule 490 (if tensor v_1 and tensor v_2 have more than one dimension and shape of v_1's dimension 0 is smaller than integer v_3, then shape of v_2 at the dimension 0 must be larger than integer v_3)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) < v_2 ∧ ndim(v_3) > 0 then shape(v_3, 0) > v_2
>>
Rule 491 (If bool v_1 is true then for all shapes of tensor v_2, the number has to smaller or equal to the min value in the tensor)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1]: shape(v_2, i) ≤ min(v_2)
>>
Rule 492 (If float v_1 is between 0 and 1, then max element in tensor v_2 is not zero.)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1 then max(v_2) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 493 (if tensor v_1 has ndim greater than 0, then tensor v_1 must satisfy that maximum element is greater than minimum element by at least a positive number v_2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then (max(v_1) + (0-min(v_1))) > v_2
>>
Rule 494 (If v_1 is a tensor with more than 1 dimensions and bool v_2 is true, then v_1 has to have a shape[0] same or greater than a value from the following list [2,4,8,16,32] )
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 ∧ v_2 then (shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 2 ∨ shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 4 ∨ shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 8 ∨ shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 16 ∨ shape(v_1, 0) ≥ 32)
>>
Rule 495 (If int v_1 is equal to zero then min of tensor v_2 has to be less than max, otherwise float v_3 must be greater than 0)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if v_1 = 0 then min(v_2) < max(v_2) else v_3 > 0
>>
Rule 496 (If float number v_1 is larger than zero, then there must exist some element in tensor v_2 such that it equals the multiplication of max and minimum value)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1]: ∃j ∈ [0, shape(v_2, i)-1] : shape(v_2, i) = max(v_2) * min(v_2)
>>
Rule 497 (If tensor v_1 is not empty, and its shape at dimension 0 is 1, then v_2 should be "constant")
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) = 1 then v_2 = "constant"
>>
Rule 498 (If bool v_1 is true, and dimension of v_2 is larger than one, shape of v_2, 0 has to be greater than v_3 AND smaller than v_4)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int, v_4 : int} |= if v_1 then ndim(v_2) > 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) > v_3 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) < v_4
>>
Rule 499 (if int v_1 is positive then there must be at least one dimension for tensor v_2 such that is shape is greater than zero or it is equal to v_1 + 5)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0 ∨ shape(v_2, i) = v_1 + 5
>>
Rule 500 (If float v_1 is between 0 and 1, then min of v_2 tensor shape[0] has to be smaller than v_1)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then shape(v_2, 0) > min(v_2)
>>
Rule 501 (If float number v_1 is non-negative, then there should exist one element in tensor v_2 such that this element is smaller than the number of dimensions from v_2)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ≥ 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1]: shape(v_2, i) < ndim(v_2)
>>
Rule 502 (If bool v_1 equals to true then maximum of tensor v_2 must be greater than 1.0 otherwise shape for all tensor v_2 dimensions must equals to 1)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 then max(v_2) > 1.0 else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2)-1]: shape(v_2, i) = 1
>>
Rule 503 (If boolean v_1 is equal to true and string v_2 is equal to "constant", then maximum and minimum of tensor v_3 should not be different)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : str, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 ∧ v_2 = "constant" then max(v_3) = min(v_3)
>>
Rule 504 (If tensor v_1 has more than 2 dimensions, then for all shape dimensions of tensor v_1, integer v_2 is less than shape value in each dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : v_2 < shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 505 (if float v_1 is not equal to 0 and tensor v_2 has positive dimension and max > 0, then the shape of its dimension 0 should be greater or equal to float v_1)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ≠ 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ max(v_2) > 0 then shape(v_2, 0) ≥ v_1
>>
Rule 506 (If string v_1 contains 'j' then dimension of v_2 tensor should be larger or equal than 2)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = "i,j->ij" ∨ v_1 = "bij,bjk->bik" ∨ v_1 = "...ij->...ji" then ndim(v_2) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 507 (If boolean v_1 equals to true then shape of dimension 0 from tensor v_2 must be not equal to integer v_3 multiplied with the maximum of tensor v_2)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= if v_1 then shape(v_2, 0) ≠ (v_3 * max(v_2))
>>
Rule 508 (Given tensor v_1, and string v_2 is one of allowed operations, the maximum shape of tensor v_1 has to greater than 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if (v_2 = "ii" ∨ v_2 = "ii->i" ∨ v_2 = "i,j->ij" ∨ v_2 = "bij,bjk->bik" ∨ v_2 = "...ij->...ji" ∨ v_2 = "bn,anm,bm->ba" ∨ v_2 = "mean" ∨ v_2 = "sum" ∨ v_2 = "max" ∨ v_2 = "constant" ∨ v_2 = "tanh") then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1)-1] : shape(v_1, i) > 1
>>
Rule 509 (if integer v_1 > 0, then exist int v_2 such that the shape in every dimension of v_3 equals to integer v_2*v_1)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∃v_3 ∈ [0, 100]: ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2)-1]: shape(v_2, i) = v_3 * v_1
>>
Rule 510 (If integer v_1 has absolute value smaller than 1 and tensor v_2 has ndim greater than 0 and greater than float v_3, then tensor v_2 should not have zero dimension)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if (v_1 < 1 ∧ v_1 > (0-1)) ∧ (ndim(v_2) > 0) ∧ (ndim(v_2) > v_3) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) ≠ 0)
>>
Rule 511 (If string v_1 is equal to "tanh" then the max shape between all dimension in tensor v_2 should be greater than float v_3)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if v_1 = "tanh" ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > v_3 )
>>
Rule 512 (If float v_1 = 1 and int v_2 = 0 then shape of all dimension for tensor v_3 should be smaller than 100)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 = 1 ∧ v_2 = 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_3) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) < 100
>>
Rule 513 (if string v_1 is 'sum' and the shape for tensor v_2 at dimension 0 is positive, then tensor v_2 ndim has to be equal to integer v_3)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= if v_1 = "sum" ∧ shape(v_2, 0) > 0 then ndim(v_2) = v_3
>>
Rule 514 (If boolean v_1 is true, and there's a tensor v_2, then every shape has to be smaller than 2, and larger than 0)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1]: shape(v_2, i) < 2 ∧ shape(v_2, i) > 0
>>
Rule 515 (if str v_1 equal to "constant" or "tanh", then min of tensor v_2 must be greater than float v_3 if it is negative and less than max if it is positive)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if (v_1 = "constant" ∨ v_1 = "tanh") ∧ (v_3 < 0) then min(v_2) > v_3 else if (v_1 = "constant" ∨ v_1 = "tanh") ∧ (v_3 > 0) then max(v_2) < v_3
>>
Rule 516 (if tensor v_1 has exactly 2 dimensions, then boolean v_2 must be true when max is greater than minimum. If it's false, then both tensors' mean and shape must be one)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then if max(v_1) > min(v_1) then v_2 else (shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) = 1)
>>
Rule 517 (If integer v_1 is 1, then 3D tensor v_2 must have this property 1, shape on the first dimension has to be greater than zero)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = 1 then ndim(v_2) = 3 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) > 0
>>
Rule 518 (Given str v_1 not equals to 'none', then given a tensor v_2 all elements has to be greater than 1)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ≠ "none" ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 1
>>
Rule 519 (Given float v_1 smaller than 10 and tensor v_2, then if string v_3 equals to "sum", then shape on 0 dimension must equal v_1 + max of tensor v_2)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if v_1 < 10 ∧ v_3 = "sum" ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then shape(v_2, 0) = (max(v_2) + v_1)
>>
Rule 520 (if the minimum and maximum of tensor v_1 is non-negative, then given int v_2 smaller than ndim of v_1, its shape at v_2 must smaller than 100)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if min(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1) then shape(v_1, v_2) < 100
>>
Rule 521 (if float v_1 is positive and less then 1, and string v_2 is 'constant', then max of tensor v_3 multiplied by v_1 must be less than 10)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : str, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 > 0 ∧ v_1 < 1 ∧ v_2 = "constant" then max(v_3) * v_1 < 10
>>
Rule 522 (If string v_1 is 'tanh' and bool v_2 is True, then shape of dimension 0 for tensor v_3 must be greater than its maximum value)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : bool, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 = "tanh" ∧ v_2 then shape(v_3, 0) > max(v_3)
>>
Rule 523 (if float v_1 is between -1 and 1 and the maximum of tensor v_2 is larger than 5, then minimum of tensor v_2 must be less than -5)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ≥ -1 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1 ∧ max(v_2) > 5 then min(v_2) < -5
>>
Rule 524 (If v_1 tensor has ndim =1, and its max value is greater than 5, then string v_2 should not be 'none'.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ max(v_1) > 5 then v_2 ≠ "none"
>>
Rule 525 (if int v_1 equals -1 then tensor v_2's ndim has to smaller than 10, and shape in the first dimension has to be greater than 1)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = -1 then ndim(v_2) < 10 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) > 1
>>
Rule 526 (If v_1 equals "...ij->...ji", and v_2 is a tensor with more than one dimension, and its shape on the first dimension is less than the maximum element on that tensor, then v_3 bool must be true)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : bool} |= if v_1 = "...ij->...ji" ∧ ndim(v_2) > 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) < max(v_2) then v_3
>>
Rule 527 (If v_1 tensor has more than one dimension and boolean v_2 is true, then the shape of dimension 0 must not be 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 ∧ v_2 then shape(v_1, 0) ≠ 1
>>
Rule 528 (If v_1 tensor's dimension is more than zero, then maximum of tensor should be equal to shape of that tensor at the dimension v_2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1) then max(v_1) = shape(v_1, v_2)
>>
Rule 529 (if string v_1 equals "...ij->...ji", then bool v_2 needs to be false or tensor v_3 shape in the first dimension must be an even number)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : bool, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 = "...ij->...ji" then v_2 = false ∨ (shape(v_3, 0) > 0 ∧ (shape(v_3, 0) / 2) * 2 = shape(v_3, 0))
>>
Rule 530 (if string v_1 equals 'constant' and tensor v_2 shape's element at index 0 smaller than 10, then its max element has to be greater than 5)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = "constant" ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) < 10 then max(v_2) > 5
>>
Rule 531 (If float v_1 is greater than 0 and equal or smaller to float v_2 and also dimension of v_3 tensor is equal to 2, then shape of 0 dimension of tensor v_3 must not be same with its shape in 1 dimension)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : float, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 > 0 ∧ v_1 ≤ v_2 ∧ ndim(v_3) = 2 then shape(v_3, 0) ≠ shape(v_3, 1)
>>
Rule 532 (if int v_1 equals 5 and float v_2 is less than 0, then shape of the first and the last dimension has to be greater than 0 for tensor v_3)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : float, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 = 5 ∧ v_2 < 0 ∧ ndim(v_3) > 0 then shape(v_3, 0) > 0 ∧ shape(v_3, ndim(v_3) - 1) > 0
>>
Rule 533 (if v_1 is float, v_2 is float and v_1 is greater than v_2, then tensor v_3 must have all elements >= 0)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : float, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 > v_2 ∧ ndim(v_3) > 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_3) - 1] : shape(v_3,i) > 0)
>>
Rule 534 (if the shape of tensor v_1 at first dimension is greater than the shape of the last dimension and string v_2 is constant, then minimum of the tensor v_1 should equal to the maximum of it)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) > shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ∧ v_2 = "constant" then min(v_1) = max(v_1)
>>
Rule 535 (If float number v_1 is greater than min(v_2) and smaller than max(v_2), then bool v_3 must be true and greater than 0 if v_2's dimension is one, or the rule is always true if it does not)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : bool} |= if min(v_2) < v_1 ∧ v_1 < max(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then (v_3 = true ∧ v_1 > 0)
>>
Rule 536 (if tensor v_1 exists and float v_2 is greater than zero, then float v_2 must be less or equal to its max value, else shape(v_1, 0) should be larger than 10)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ v_2 > 0 then v_2 ≤ max(v_1) else if shape(v_1, 0) < 10 then true
>>
Rule 537 (If tensor v_1's shape at index 0 is greater than float v_2 and v_3 boolean is true, then shape v_1's last dimension has to be one of the supported output shapes)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float, v_3 : bool} |= if shape(v_1, 0) > v_2 ∧ ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ v_3 then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 2 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 4 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 8 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = 16
>>
Rule 538 (If float v_1 is less than min(v_2), then the minimum of v_2 tensor must be equal to the integer v_3 and tensor should has a dimension > 0)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= if v_1 < min(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then min(v_2) = v_3
>>
Rule 539 (If v_1 is bool and is true, and the tensor v_2 is not empty, then the min of v_2 must smaller or equal to its max)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0) then min(v_2) ≤ max(v_2)
>>
Rule 540 (If integer v_1 is greater than 0, and there exist some dimensions with shape in tensor v_2 smaller than or equal to 5, the string v_3 should equals 'tanh')
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if v_1 > 0 ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) ≤ 5) then v_3 = "tanh"
>>
Rule 541 (If tensor v_1 and v_2 have more than zero dimensions, then max(v_1) must be less or equal than min(v_2))
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then max(v_1) ≤ min(v_2)
>>
Rule 542 (If tensor v_1 has dimension greater than 0, then min of v_1 must be either greater than 0 or less than float v_2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then min(v_1) > 0 ∨ min(v_1) < v_2
>>
Rule 543 (If bool v_1 is false, then if tensor v_2's ndim is positive then both max and min value of tensor v_2 should be smaller than integer v_3)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= if v_1 = false ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then max(v_2) < v_3 ∧ min(v_2) < v_3
>>
Rule 544 (if integer v_1 is equal to 0, then for 2 dimension tensor v_2, shape at its both dimensions must be smaller than float number v_3 )
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if v_1 = 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 2 then shape(v_2, 0) < v_3 ∧ shape(v_2, 1) < v_3
>>
Rule 545 (if str v_1 contains only "i" (and is not empty) AND tensor v_2 contains more than zero dimensions, then its dimension must be 1, and the multiplication of shape at 0 times max value has to be less than 10000.)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor} |= if (v_1 = "ii" ∨ v_1 = "ii->i") ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ndim(v_2) = 1 ∧ (shape(v_2, 0) * max(v_2)) < 10000
>>
Rule 546 (if boolean v_1 equals true, then shape of every dimension of tensor v_2 must be greater than float v_3 and smaller than float v_4)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float, v_4 : float} |= if v_1 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2)-1]: shape(v_2, i) > v_3 ∧ shape(v_2, i) < v_4
>>
Rule 547 (If string v_1 is tanh, then the difference between its min and max value must be smaller than float v_2)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if v_1 = "tanh" ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then (max(v_2) - min(v_2)) < v_3
>>
Rule 548 (If the sum of minimum and maximum of the tensor v_1 is greater than 0 and tensor v_1 is empty, then str v_2 has to equal to 'none')
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if (min(v_1) + (0-max(v_1))) > 0 ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0) then v_2 = "none"
>>
Rule 549 (If int v_1 is less than 0 then each value of the shape of tensor v_2 in each dimension should be less than float number v_3)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if v_1 < 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) < v_3
>>
Rule 550 (If the dimension of v_1 is greater than zero and there is one element where tensor's shape equals to 10, then string v_2 should be 'constant')
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 0) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1)-1]: shape(v_1, i) = 10) then v_2 = "constant"
>>
Rule 551 (If tensor v_1 is not empty and the string v_2 does not equal 'none', then the shape of v_1 at the last dimension should not equal shape of v_1 at the second last dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) ∧ v_2 ≠ "none" ∧ ndim(v_1) > 1 then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) -1 ) ≠ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2)
>>
Rule 552 (If str v_1 is not "none" and tensor v_2 is not empty, then its maximum has to be larger than the minimum by float v_3 value )
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if v_1 ≠ "none" ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) > 0) then (max(v_2) + (0-min(v_2))) > v_3
>>
Rule 553 (If int v_1 is greater than -1 and dimension of v_2 tensor is greater than 0, then v_1 + shape in the first dimension should not be greater than 10)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 > -1 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then (v_1 + shape(v_2, 0)) < 10
>>
Rule 554 (if float v_1 is between -1 and 1, and v_2 string does not equal to none, then there has to exists one dimension of tensor v_3 such that is shape is equal to int 1)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : str, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 ≥ -1 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1 ∧ v_2 ≠ "none" ∧ ndim(v_3) > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_3) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = 1
>>
Rule 555 (If bool v_1 is True, float v_2 has shape less than 100 then tensor v_3 has one dimension where its shape is equal to int 5)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : float, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 ∧ v_2 < 100 ∧ ndim(v_3) > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_3) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) = 5
>>
Rule 556 (if tensor v_1 has ndim greater than float number 2 and shape on first dimension is smaller than second dimension, then string v_2 should not be equal to max)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) < shape(v_1, 1) then v_2 ≠ "max"
>>
Rule 557 (if float v_1 is less than zero and tensor v_2 has dimension shape(0) < shape(1), then the string should not be equal to 'tanh')
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if v_1 < 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 1 ∧ shape(v_2, 0) < shape(v_2, 1) then v_3 ≠ "tanh"
>>
Rule 558 (if float number v_1 is less than min value in tensor v_2, then string v_3 must be 'constant' or float v_1 must smaller than -10)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if v_1 < min(v_2) then v_3 = "constant" ∨ v_1 < -10
>>
Rule 559 (If float v_1 > 0 then for all dimensions i in tensor v_2, shape has to be either same with the last dimension or max element smaller than integer 1000)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 > 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : (shape(v_2, i) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2)-1)) ∨ (max(v_2) < 1000)
>>
Rule 560 (If string v_1 is equal to tanh and float v_2 is greater than 1, then at least one shape for tensor v_3 has to be greater than 0.)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : float, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 = "tanh" ∧ v_2 > 1 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_3) - 1] : shape(v_3, i) > 0
>>
Rule 561 (If the max element of tensor v_1 smaller than the min element of tensor v_2, and also these tensor are different, then boolean v_3 must be false)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : bool} |= if max(v_1) < min(v_2) ∧ v_1 ≠ v_2 then v_3 = false
>>
Rule 562 (If the dimension of v_1 tensor is less than integer v_2, and string v_3 is 'sum', then shape of the dimension 0 of the tensor v_1 must be equal to integer 5)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : str} |= if ndim(v_1) < v_2 ∧ ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ v_3 = "sum" then shape(v_1, 0) = 5
>>
Rule 563 (If tensor v_1 is not empty and not a scalar, then shape of all the dimension are not equal to integer v_2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ v_2)
>>
Rule 564 (If float number v_1 is greater than max of tensor v_2, and tensor v_2 has at least 1 dimensions, then String v_3 must equal to "tanh" if v_1 is smaller than 100)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if (v_1 > max(v_2)) ∧ (ndim(v_2) > 0) ∧ (v_1 < 100) then v_3 = "tanh"
>>
Rule 565 (if boolean v_1 is false, then the result of multiplication between min and max value for tensor v_2 must be greater than integer 100)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = false ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then min(v_2) * max(v_2) > 10
>>
Rule 566 (If v_1 has more than one dimension and int v_2 is a valid index on v_1 then float v_3 must greater than value 5 and smaller or equal to value of shape(v_1, v_2) )
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : float} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 ∧ v_2 ≥ (0 - ndim(v_1)) ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1) then v_3 > 5 ∧ v_3 ≤ shape(v_1, v_2)
