>>
Rule 616 (If float v_1 and float v_2 sum up to zero and tensor v_3 has dimension greater than zero then min of the tensor must be larger than v_1)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 + v_2 = 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then min(v_2) > v_1
>>
Rule 617 (If bool v_1 is true, then if there exists a float v_2 in tensor v_3 then that v_2 float number must be less than value 5)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) < 5
>>
Rule 618 (If tensor v_1 has more than 2 dimensions and float v_2 is equal to 0.3, then shape of v_1 at the last dimension has to be equal shape of v_1 at the second to last dimension divided by 2)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 ∧ v_2 = 0.3 then shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2) / 2
