Rule 620 (If float v_1 is equal or greater than the max value and smaller than sum of shape from first and second dimension (and greater than 1) of tensor v_2 with at least two dimension, string v_3 is not "none", then bool v_4 has to be false)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str, v_4 : bool} |= if v_1 ≥ max(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_2) ≥ 2 ∧ v_1 < (shape(v_2, 0) + shape(v_2, 1)) ∧ v_1 > 1 ∧ v_3 ≠ "none" then v_4 = false
>>
Rule 621 (If the result of the multiplication between float number v_1 and float number v_2 is less than one and the tensor v_3 has positive dimensions, then the minimum value of that tensor should be greater than -10)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor} |= if (v_1 * (if max(v_2) < 0 then 0-max(v_2) else max(v_2))) < 1 then ndim(v_2) > 0 ∧ min(v_2) > -10
>>
Rule 622 (If v_1 is equal to 0, then the result of the difference between tensor v_2 maximum shape and the multiplication of integer v_3 with two must be greater than zero)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= if v_1 = 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then (max(v_2) - (v_3 * 2)) > 0
>>
Rule 623 (If integer v_1 is equal 0, string v_2 is equal "none" or float v_3 is equal to 0.0, then the maximum dimension of tensor v_4 shape must be larger or equal to 0)
{v_1 : int, v_2 : str, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 = 0 ∧ (v_2 = "none" ∨ v_3 = 0.0) then max(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 624 (Given v_1 as string and v_2 as a tensor. If v_1 contains 'bjk', then product of last two shapes for v_2 should be greater than integer 10)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor} |= if (v_1 = "bij,bjk->bik" ∨ v_1 = "bjk->bik") ∧ (ndim(v_2) > 1) then (shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 1) * shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - 2)) > 10
>>
Rule 625 (If v_1 is true and v_2 string has length > 2, then the max of tensor should be greater than 5)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : str, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 ∧ (shape(v_2,0) > 2) ∧ ndim(v_3) > 0 then max(v_3) > 5
>>
Rule 626 (if string v_1 is 'ii' or 'ii->i', then tensor v_2 must have at least 1 dimension with shape equals to float number v_3 and it's max element has to be larger than 0)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : float} |= if (v_1 = "ii" ∨ v_1 = "ii->i") ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = v_3 ∧ max(v_2) > 0
>>
Rule 627 (if bool v_1 equals to True, then there exists a dimension in tensor v_2 where the value of the shape in this dimension and all values are divisible by 2)
{v_1 : bool, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) / 2 = 0
>>
Rule 628 (If string v_1 is 'tanh' and integer v_2 = 1, then minimum element of tensor v_3 has to be greater than -10 and less than 1)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : int, v_3 : tensor} |= if v_1 = "tanh" ∧ v_2 = 1 ∧ ndim(v_3) > 0 then min(v_3) > -10 ∧ min(v_3) < 1
>>
Rule 629 (If float v_1 has absolute value greater than 1 and ndim of tensor v_2 is positive, then the shape of v_2 dimension 0 has to smaller than 100, or string v_3 must be mean)
{v_1 : float, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : str} |= if (if v_1 < 0 then 0 - v_1 else v_1) > 1 ∧ ndim(v_2) > 0 then shape(v_2, 0) < 100 ∨ v_3 = "mean"
>>
Rule 630 (The size of input tensor should be greater than the given number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= shape(v_1, 0) > v_2
>>
Rule 631 (If a tensor has more than one dimension, then the given dimension index should be valid)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 632 (If a string is "sum" or "mean" then the input tensor should have more than one dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if v_2 = "sum" ∨ v_2 = "mean" then ndim(v_1) > 1
>>
Rule 633 (If the string is not "none", then the input tensor should have more than zero dimension.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if v_2 ≠ "none" then ndim(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 634 (Two tensors should have same shape along specific dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : int} |= shape(v_1, v_3) = shape(v_2, v_3)
>>
Rule 635 (If a tensor has more than two dimensions, then minimum value must be smaller than maximum)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 then min(v_1) ≤ max(v_1)
>>
Rule 636 (If a tensor has three dimensions, then the sum of shape in dimension 0 and dimension 1 should be smaller than shape in dimension 2)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 then shape(v_1, 0) + shape(v_1, 1) ≤ shape(v_1, 2)
>>
Rule 637 (If a string is "tanh", then the minimum value should be greater than -1 and the maximum value should be less than 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if v_2 = "tanh" then min(v_1) ≥ -1 ∧ max(v_1) ≤ 1
>>
Rule 638 (If a tensor is 1-dimensional, its shape should be smaller than the given number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then shape(v_1, 0) < v_2
>>
Rule 639 (if the tensor is 2-dimensional, shape[0] should be equal to shape[1])
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 640 (If a boolean variable is true, then the input tensor must be 3-dimensional)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : bool} |= if v_2 = true then ndim(v_1) = 3
>>
Rule 641 (For a 2D tensor, the sum of all elements must be greater than a given number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : min(v_1) * shape(v_1, 0) * shape(v_1, 1) > v_2
>>
Rule 642 (If the string is "constant", then the shape of the input tensor in all dimensions should be 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if v_2 = "constant" then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1
>>
Rule 643 (The value of integer variable should be in range 0 to the product of tensor's shape.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= 0 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i))
>>
Rule 644 (The size of the first dimension of the input tensor must be a multiple of given number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= shape(v_1, 0) / v_2 = (shape(v_1, 0) + 1 - 1) / v_2
>>
Rule 645 (if the second dimension of a tensor is smaller than 10, the first dimension must have size 1)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) < 10 then shape(v_1, 0) = 1
