Rule 646 (If the input tensor has more than 1 dimension, then its minimum value should be non-negative.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then min(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 647 (The first two dimensions of input tensor should be equal)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 648 (If the given integer is 0, the tensor can have any shape; if the given integer is 1, the tensor must be a vector)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if v_2 = 0 then true else if v_2 = 1 then ndim(v_1) = 1 else false
>>
Rule 649 (If the minimum value of the tensor is greater than the maximum value, then the tensor must be empty)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if min(v_1) > max(v_1) then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0
>>
Rule 650 (The maximum value of the tensor must be greater than the given floating-point number)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : float} |= max(v_1) > v_2
>>
