Rule 804 (if the tensor is at least 2-dimensional and the first element is greater than 0, then the string must not be 'none')
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: str} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ min(v_1) > 0 then v_2 ≠ "none"
>>
Rule 805 (If string equals to one of the following: ["ii->i", "i,j->ij", "bij,bjk->bik", "...ij->...ji", "bn,anm,bm->ba"] then tensor should have at least one dimension)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 = "ii->i" ∨ v_2 = "i,j->ij" ∨ v_2 = "bij,bjk->bik" ∨ v_2 = "...ij->...ji" ∨ v_2 = "bn,anm,bm->ba" then ndim(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 806 (If the string is one of the following: 'ii->i', 'i,j->ij', 'bij,bjk->bik',then tensor must have at least two dimensions.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : str} |= if v_2 = "ii->i" ∨ v_2 = "i,j->ij" ∨ v_2 = "bij,bjk->bik" then ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 807 (If input tensor has two dimension and the given string is not 'none' and its minimum value equals to zero, then its maximum value must be positive.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (v_2 ≠ "none") ∧ (min(v_1) = 0) then max(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 808 (if string equals to "tanh", max shape dimension must be smaller than 2000)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 = "tanh" then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) < 2000
>>
Rule 809 (if input tensor v_1's ndim is greater than zero and its dtype is an integer, all elements of v_1 should be greater or equals to zero)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 0) ∧ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) then (∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : v_1 ≥ 0)
>>
Rule 810 (If the number of dimensions for input is 2, the shape[0] has to be a prime number)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then  ∀i ∈ [2, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : shape(v_1, 0) / i ≠ (shape(v_1, 0) + 1 -1) / i
>>
Rule 811 (if the input tensor is more than 2 dimensions, its minimum element must be less than its maximum element. )
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 then min(v_1) < max(v_1)
>>
Rule 812 (if the tensor v_1 is 1D, it's minimum shape must be equal to its maximum shape)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then shape(v_1, 0) = max(v_1)
>>
Rule 813 (if v_2 is set to “tanh”, then min element in tensor v_1 should not be equals to or larger than 0)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (v_2 = "tanh") then min(v_1) < 0
>>
Rule 814 (If the tensor has ndim = 3 and string equals 'bij,bjk->bik' then, shape(v_1,1) has to be equal shape(v_2,0) and shape(v_2,1) = shape(v_3,0)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor, v_4: str} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 ∧ v_4 = "bij,bjk->bik" then shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_2, 0) ∧ shape(v_2, 1) = shape(v_3, 0)
>>
Rule 815 (If the string parameter is "tanh", all shapes must be greater than 1 and the values in tensor v_1 should all be unique.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 = "tanh" then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 1) ∧ (∀x ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1]: ∀y ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1]: (∃a ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1]: ∃b ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : (x ≠ a ∨ y ≠ b) ∧ v_1 ≠ v_1))
>>
Rule 816 (if ndim of v_1 is equal to 1 and max shape dimension < 10, then string must not equal to mean.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 1) ∧ (shape(v_1, 0) < 10) then v_2 ≠ "mean"
>>
Rule 817 (if ndim is greater than or equal to 1 and if its dtype is a number type, then it needs to have non-zero value somewhere)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) ≥ 1) ∧ ((1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) ∨ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8)) then ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : v_1 ≠ 0
>>
Rule 818 (If the input tensor has dtype as bool all elements must be equal)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 0) then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : (v_1 = true) ∨ (v_1 = false)
>>
Rule 819 (If the shape of tensor v_1 at dim 0 is smaller than 10, then its min value must be 0.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if shape(v_1, 0) < 10 then min(v_1) = 0
>>
Rule 820 (If ndim(v_1) > 0 then ∃ i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) -1] , shape(v_1, i) should be an odd number.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, i) / 2 ≠ (shape(v_1, i) + 1 - 1) / 2)
>>
Rule 821 (If string equals to "constant", then any value of a tensor should be either zero or one)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 = "constant" then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : (v_1 = 1 ∨ v_1 = 0)
>>
Rule 822 (If number of dimensions of the tensor equals 2 and tensor's minimum value equals to 0, then string should not equal to tanh)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (min(v_1) = 0) then v_2 ≠ "tanh"
>>
Rule 823 (If the shape of first dimension is bigger than 5, and string is sum or mean or max, then dtype has to be float or complex)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (shape(v_1, 0) > 5) ∧ (v_2 = "sum" ∨ v_2 = "mean" ∨ v_2 = "max") then (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10)
>>
Rule 824 (if the input tensor's data type is integer and its ndim is 2, the max value can't be equal to min value)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) ∧ ndim(v_1) = 2 then max(v_1) ≠ min(v_1)
>>
Rule 825 (If string v_2 is 'tanh', then tensor v_1's all shapes has to smaller than or equal to 20)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 = "tanh" then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≤ 20
>>
Rule 826 (If tensor v_1's number of dimensions is equal to 1 and dtype is float, the multiplication of its elements should be a number smaller than 10)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : v_1 * shape(v_1, 0) < 10
>>
Rule 827 (If ndim = 2, the shape (0) must be greater than the max and the dtype should either be boolean or string)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) then (shape(v_1, 0) > max(v_1)) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11)
>>
Rule 828 (if tensor has shape equal to (1,1) and its dtype is bool or int, then its max value must be less than 2)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (shape(v_1, 0) = 1 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) = 1) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 0 ∨ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) then max(v_1) < 2
>>
Rule 829 (For a two-dimensional tensor with float-type values and v_2 equals to "tanh", the difference between its shape dimensions must not be divisible by a prime number)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∧ v_2 = "tanh" then ∀i ∈ [2, shape(v_1, 0) - shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : (shape(v_1, 0) - shape(v_1, 1)) / i ≠ ((shape(v_1, 0) - shape(v_1, 1)) + 1 - 1) / i
>>
Rule 830 (If string v_2 is equal to 'mean', and if min of tensor is less than 0, then max of v_1 must be greater than 0 and vice versa)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 = "mean" then if min(v_1) < 0 then max(v_1) > 0 else if max(v_1) > 0 then min(v_1) < 0
>>
Rule 831 (If ndim of the tensor is greater than zero, and string equals max, then for any one dimension shape of the tensor in that dimension > 1)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 0) ∧ (v_2 = "max") then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) > 1
>>
Rule 832 (If ndim of tensor v_1 is equal to 3 then the all shapes must be equal.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 then shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1) ∧ shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_1, 2)
>>
Rule 833 (if ndim of tensor is smaller than 3 and dtype is a float type, then min of tensor has to be less than its shape.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) < 3) ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then min(v_1) < shape(v_1, 0)
>>
Rule 834 (if tensor v_1 has a number of dimensions equal to 1, all of the elements on that tensor must be less than or equal to the floating point number that is bound to variable v_2)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: float} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 1) then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1]: v_1 ≤ v_2
>>
Rule 835 (If the input tensor v_1 number of dimensions equals 2, then shape(v_1, 0) should be equal to min(v_1) + max(v_1))
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 0) = min(v_1) + max(v_1)
>>
Rule 836 (if the tensor shape in 0th dimension is 1 and string is tanh then maximum value must be positive and less than 1)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (shape(v_1, 0) = 1) ∧ (v_2 = "tanh") then (max(v_1) > 0) ∧ (max(v_1) < 1)
>>
Rule 837 (If tensor has shape equal to (1,1), then its max and min element have to have different signs)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (shape(v_1, 0) = 1) ∧ (shape(v_1, 1) = 1) then max(v_1) > 0 ∧ min(v_1) < 0
>>
Rule 838 (If the tensor has number of dimensions equals 2, data type must be float, and string isn't "none", then all elements should be smaller than 10000 and bigger than -10000.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∧ (v_2 ≠ "none") then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : v_1 < 10000 ∧ v_1 > -10000
>>
Rule 839 (if the input tensor's shape dimensions are equal, then the product of all shapes must be greater or equal to min(tensor))
{v_1: tensor} |= if (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [i+1, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_1, j)) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i)) ≥ min(v_1)
>>
Rule 840 (If a bool is true and string is none, the product of shapes must be zero)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: bool, v_3: str} |= if (v_2 = true) ∧ (v_3 = "none") then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0
>>
Rule 841 (If the tensor number of dimensions is 3, then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] the max value of the tensor equals its shape )
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 3 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) = max(v_1)
>>
Rule 842 (If a tensor has more than one dimension, then the average of its shape should be a positive number)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i)) / ndim(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 843 (If the number of dimension is equal to 2, at least one of its max elements should be smaller than 100 or at least one shape dimension should be 1)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then ∃i ∈ [0, 1] : (max(v_1) < 100 ∨ shape(v_1, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 844 (If ndim of tensor v_1 is greater than 2, and max > 0, then string cannot be 'none' and also shape of the dimensions has to be greater than zero.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 2) ∧ (max(v_1) > 0) then (v_2 ≠ "none") ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0)
>>
Rule 845 (if ndim is 3 and dtype is a union of int or string, then shape 1 and shape 2 can't be the same)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 3) ∧ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11) then shape(v_1, 1) ≠ shape(v_1, 2)
>>
Rule 846 (If dtype is "float" and the shape dimension equals one then it must be > 1000)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 1) then shape(v_1, 0) > 1000
>>
Rule 847 (If the string parameter is not 'none' then the value (min+max) of the tensor v_1 must equal a constant number 10 or number of dimensions should be less than 2)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 ≠ "none" then (min(v_1) + max(v_1) = 10) ∨ ndim(v_1) < 2
>>
Rule 848 (For a given tensor v_1, if it has two dimensions, then maximum value of v_1 has to be greater than shape(0) + shape(1) and has to have a dtype int.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) then max(v_1) > shape(v_1, 0) + shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 849 (If v_2 string not equal 'none' and tensor has number of dimension equal to 4, then all elements must positive and the product of its shape dimensions has to bigger than 10)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 4) ∧ (v_2 ≠ "none") then ((∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i)) > 10) ∧ (min(v_1) > 0)
>>
Rule 850 (if input tensor is empty, the string has to equal to 'none')
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0 then v_2 = "none"
>>
Rule 851 (If the data type is string and number of dimension is bigger than 0, the string must be a value included in the following string values)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 11) ∧ (ndim(v_1) > 0) then ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0)-1]: (v_1 = "ii" ∨ v_1 = "ii->i" ∨ v_1 = "i,j->ij" ∨ v_1 = "bij,bjk->bik" ∨ v_1 = "...ij->...ji" ∨ v_1 = "bn,anm,bm->ba" ∨ v_1 = "none" ∨ v_1 = "mean" ∨ v_1 = "sum" ∨ v_1 = "max" ∨ v_1 = "constant" ∨ v_1 = "tanh")
>>
Rule 852 (If tensor has more than 1 dimension and shape of 0th dim is larger then 1000, its dtype cannot be bool)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (shape(v_1, 0) > 1000) then dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 853 (For all tensors v_1 and v_2, if their ndim is > 1, the min of both tensors must be equal to each other)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (ndim(v_2) > 1) then min(v_1) = min(v_2)
>>
Rule 854 (If the number of dimension of input tensor is less than 3, then all values must lie within the range of minimum and maximum limits of dtype integer)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) < 3 then ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : if dtype_(v_1) = 1 then -128 ≤ v_1 ∧ v_1 ≤ 127 else if dtype_(v_1) = 2 then -32768 ≤ v_1 ∧ v_1 ≤ 32767 else if dtype_(v_1) = 3 then -2147483648 ≤ v_1 ∧ v_1 ≤ 2147483647 else if dtype_(v_1) = 4 then -9223372036854775808 ≤ v_1 ∧ v_1 ≤ 9223372036854775807 else if dtype_(v_1) = 5 then 0 ≤ v_1 ∧ v_1 ≤ 255
>>
Rule 855 (if tensor's shape in dimension 0 equal 1, its minimum and maximum value must satisfy this: (maximum value + minimum value = 1 or 0) )
{v_1: tensor} |= if (shape(v_1, 0) = 1) then (min(v_1) + max(v_1) = 1) ∨ (min(v_1) + max(v_1) = 0)
>>
Rule 856 (If the dtype of the input tensor v_1 is complex64, then maximum value of real part must be greater than the minimum value of imaginary part)
{v_1: tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 9 then max(v_1) > min(v_1)
>>
Rule 857 (If string v_2 equals to "ii", then the input v_1 should be 2D tensor and the product of its shape has to equal to min times 2 and the dtype shoul be integer )
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (v_2 = "ii") ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) then shape(v_1, 0) * shape(v_1, 1) = 2 * min(v_1)
>>
Rule 858 (If string v_2 does not equal to "tanh", and the shape of dimension zero of tensor v_1 is less than 100, then the maximum element of v_1 is greater than or equal to 1)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 ≠ "tanh" ∧ shape(v_1, 0) < 100 then max(v_1) ≥ 1
>>
Rule 859 (If tensor v_1 has number of dimensions greater than one and a shape equals to 1, and it's a float tensor, string must be tanh.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1)-1]: shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then "tanh" < v_1
>>
Rule 860 (If tensor v_1 has two dimensions, if string v_2 is "sum", first shape must not be equal to the second one.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (v_2 = "sum") then shape(v_1, 0) ≠ shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 861 (if tensor's ndim >=3 and type is float, sum of all shapes should be smaller than 10000)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) ≥ 3) ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then (shape(v_1, 0) + shape(v_1, 1) + shape(v_1, 2)) < 10000
>>
Rule 862 (If string equals "tanh", and tensor has number of dimensions more than 1, and min < 0, all shapes must be > 1)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (v_2 = "tanh") ∧ (min(v_1) < 0) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) > 1
>>
Rule 863 (If tensor has at least one dimension, shape of its zero'th dimension should be less than the product of its min value and number 1000)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 then shape(v_1, 0) < (min(v_1) * 1000)
>>
Rule 864 (If the dtype is bool, max value == min value and greater than max value of the float tensor)
{v_1: tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 0) then max(v_1) = min(v_1) ∧ max(v_1) > max(v_2)
>>
Rule 865 (If ndim(v_1) = 2 and v_2 (string) is "mean" , then all shapes must equal one and data type cannot be float 64)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (v_2 = "mean") then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) = 1) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 8)
>>
Rule 866 (If number of dimension of tensor v_1 is greater than 1 and minimum number in this tensor is less than 0, then if string v_2 is equal to max then all the shapes must be not equal to 100)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (min(v_1) < 0) ∧ (v_2 = "max") then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, i) ≠ 100
>>
Rule 867 (For a tensor with boolean values, then either its maximum value or its minimum value must be 0.)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 0) then max(v_1) = 0 ∨ min(v_1) = 0
>>
Rule 868 (If string equals to 'bn,anm,bm->ba' then the shapes of v_1,v_2,v_3 has to satisfy shape(v_1,0) = shape(v_2,0) and shape(v_2,2) = shape(v_3,0))
{v_1 : tensor, v_2: tensor, v_3: tensor, v_4: str} |= if (v_4 = "bn,anm,bm->ba") then (shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_2, 0)) ∧ (shape(v_2, 2) = shape(v_3, 0))
>>
Rule 869 (If the string parameter equals "sum", then the tensor's minimum value squared must be less than the maximum value squared)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 = "sum" then (min(v_1) * min(v_1)) < (max(v_1) * max(v_1))
>>
Rule 870 (If a tensor has a shape greater than 10000, then it needs to be one dimensional)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 10000 then ndim(v_1) = 1
>>
Rule 871 (If the maximum element is equal to 0, all of its elements must also be zero)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if max(v_1) = 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : v_1 = 0
>>
Rule 872 (If the tensor's ndim is 3 and its shape at dimensions 0, 1, and 2 are same and dtype is string, it cannot be equal to 'constant')
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 3) ∧ (shape(v_1, 0) = shape(v_1, 1) ∧ shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_1, 2)) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 11) then v_1 ≠ "constant"
>>
Rule 873 (If a 1-D tensor has a float data type, then all the shape must be same with its minimum value plus maximum value multiplied by 0.5)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 1) ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = (min(v_1) + max(v_1)) * 0.5
>>
Rule 874 (if the input tensor v_1 has more than one dimension, then its max * min value must be greater or equal to -100)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then max(v_1) * min(v_1) ≥ -100
>>
Rule 875 (If the string equals to sum and tensor has number of dimensions larger than 1 and type is in, then max value can't be smaller than product of shape of that tensor divided by 2)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (v_2 = "sum") ∧ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) then max(v_1) ≥ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i))/2
>>
Rule 876 (If the input tensor v_1 has more than 2 dimension, the multiplication between minimum shape and maximum shape > 100)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) * shape(v_1, j) > 100)
>>
Rule 877 (If tensor shape on the first dimension equal to 1 and its dtype not complex64 or complex128, and tensor's ndim smaller than 3, then string v_2 must be equal to 'constant' or equal to 'none')
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (shape(v_1, 0) = 1) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 9 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 10) ∧ (ndim(v_1) < 3) then (v_2 = "constant") ∨ (v_2 = "none")
>>
Rule 878 (If the shape of input tensor is (1,1) then the string MUST be equal to constant)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 0) ∧ (shape(v_1, 0) = 1) ∧ (shape(v_1, 1) = 1) then v_2 = "constant"
>>
Rule 879 (If the input tensor has the same shape on all dimensions and the string is not 'none' then the maximum value in the tensor must be grater than its shape)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [i+1, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_1, j)) ∧ (v_2 ≠ "none") then max(v_1) > shape(v_1, 0)
>>
Rule 880 (For a 2D tensor if sum of shapes is an odd number, the string should not be 'constant')
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ ((shape(v_1, 0) + shape(v_1, 1))/2 ≠ ((shape(v_1, 0) + shape(v_1, 1)) + 1 - 1)/2) then v_2 ≠ "constant"
>>
Rule 881 (If shape of any dimension of the tensor is less than its max and less than its min, string has to be "none" )
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) < min(v_1)) ∧ (∃j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, j) < max(v_1)) then v_2 = "none"
>>
Rule 882 (If the number of shape dimensions > 0 then there should be at least one element, i, in the tensor v1 to satisfy these two conditions v1 > shape(0) and string must be "tanh".)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if ndim(v_1) > 0 then (∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∃j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : v_1 > shape(v_1, 0) ∧ v_2 = "tanh")
>>
Rule 883 (If shape of tensor equals to (2,2) and dtype of it is string, the value can either be equal to none or constant)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (shape(v_1, 0) = 2 ∧ shape(v_1, 1) = 2) ∧ dtype_(v_1) = 11 then (v_1 = "none") ∨ (v_1 = "constant")
>>
Rule 884 (if the number of dimensions of input v_1 tensor equal 2, then its max shape <= 6 and it's min should be greater than 10)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≤ 6) ∧ (min(v_1) > 10)
>>
Rule 885 (If v_1 type is str, v_1 should be one of those, and dtype of all tensors has to be same )
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 11 then (∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0)-1]: (v_1 = "ii" ∨ v_1 = "ii->i" ∨ v_1 = "i,j->ij" ∨ v_1 = "bij,bjk->bik" ∨ v_1 = "...ij->...ji" ∨ v_1 = "bn,anm,bm->ba" ∨ v_1 = "none" ∨ v_1 = "mean" ∨ v_1 = "sum" ∨ v_1 = "max" ∨ v_1 = "constant" ∨ v_1 = "tanh")) ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 886 (if the tensor v_1 is 2 dimensional and the maximum shape between v_1 and v_2 is higher than 10 and the string "mean" is used ,the data type must be a float tensor)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ ((shape(v_1, 0) > 10 ∨ shape(v_1, 1) > 10)) ∧ (v_2 = "mean") then (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8)
>>
Rule 887 (if the number of dimensions is 1, then max of input should be smaller than 100 or the input should be of boolean type )
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then max(v_1) < 100 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 0
>>
Rule 888 (if dtype is str, then minimum value of v_1 is greater than shape value on 0th dimension)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 11) then min(v_1) > shape(v_1, 0)
>>
Rule 889 (If the ndim of a tensor equal 1, then its maximum or minimum value must be smaller than or equal to 100.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then (min(v_1) ≤ 100) ∨ (max(v_1) ≤ 100)
>>
Rule 890 (If string is sum, and if min is greater than 0 all dimensions must have odd shape)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (v_2 = "sum") ∧ (min(v_1) > 0) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) / 2 ≠ ((shape(v_1, i) + 1 - 1) / 2)
>>
Rule 891 (If tensor is 3D and string equals to constant, then its elements should be positive and between 0 to 1)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 3) ∧ (v_2 = "constant") then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : v_1 > 0 ∧ v_1 < 1
>>
Rule 892 (if the input is at least one dimensional and has float dtype, the shape of its first dimension should be an integer that satisfy the following conditions, being more than 50 and less than 100. )
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) >= 1) ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then shape(v_1, 0) > 50 ∧ shape(v_1, 0) < 100
>>
Rule 893 (if number of dimensions is equal to 2 and tensor type is boolean, the max cannot be greater than min.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 0) then max(v_1) ≤ min(v_1)
>>
Rule 894 (if string equals to "sum", then tensor v_1 shape(0) must be greater than 1, or its max element must less than 0)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 = "sum" then (shape(v_1, 0) > 1) ∨ (max(v_1) < 0)
>>
Rule 895 (if v_1's dtype is float type and the string "tanh" is the given string, v_1 shape should only be made of ones and number of dimensions must be equal to 2)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∧ (v_2 = "tanh") then (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 1)
>>
Rule 896 (If tensor data type is string, then its length must smaller than 50)
{v_1: tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 11 then shape(v_1, 0) < 50
>>
Rule 897 (If string is not "none" and tensor type is not boolean, min(tensor) has to be a number and greater than zero and minimum value can't be different to maximum value)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (v_2 ≠ "none") ∧ (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0) then (min(v_1) ≥ 0) ∧ (min(v_1) ≠ max(v_1))
>>
Rule 898 (If the tensor has a floating point data type and two dimension it needs all values to be in the range between -1 and 1)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∧ ndim(v_1) = 2 then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : v_1 ≥ -1 ∧ v_1 ≤ 1
>>
Rule 899 (If input is 2-dimensional and dtype is an integer type, then the product of minimum value and maximum value should be positive)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) then min(v_1) * max(v_1) > 0
>>
Rule 900 (if the tensor is at least a 1D tensor with boolean data type, at least one value equals 'true' or 'false')
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) >= 1) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 0) then (∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) -1]: v_1 = true) ∨ (∃j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1]: v_1 = false)
>>
Rule 901 (If a tensor has three dimensions and its dtype is a union of int and float, then there exists a shape equal to min.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 3) ∧ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = min(v_1)
>>
Rule 902 ( if the tensor v_1's number of dimensions is 2 and the string equals tanh, the values in its first row must be smaller or equals 1 and its shapes must not be 0)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (v_2 = "tanh") then (∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : v_1 ≤ 1) ∧ (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0)
>>
Rule 903 (if the tensor has more than one dimension and its data type is float, the maximum of the shapes must be smaller than 50)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) < 50
>>
Rule 904 (If the input tensor is 3 dimensional, its max, min, and a bool variable equal to true, then max value should be positive and minimum negative.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: bool} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 3) ∧ (v_2 = true) then (max(v_1) > 0) ∧ (min(v_1) < 0)
>>
Rule 905 (for the input tensors if number of dimensions is at least 1 and its of int or float type the min(v_1)+max(v_1) > 0, if the v_2 a boolean variable equals true)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: bool} |= if (ndim(v_1) ≥ 1) ∧ ((1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) ∨ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8)) ∧ (v_2 = true) then (min(v_1) + max(v_1) > 0)
>>
Rule 906 (If a tensor is 1-dimensional its max element must be less then 10 and its data type should be "float" or "int".)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then max(v_1) < 10 ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8 ∨ 1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5)
>>
Rule 907 (If string equal sum or mean, maximum value should be greather than 0.01 and minimum value should be less than 0)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (v_2 = "sum" ∨ v_2 = "mean") then max(v_1) > 0.01 ∧ min(v_1) < 0
>>
Rule 908 (if number of dimension is smaller than 4 for input v_1, and string equal to 'tanh', the max(v_1)+min(v_1) has to smaller or equal to zero)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) < 4) ∧ (v_2 = "tanh") then max(v_1) + min(v_1) ≤ 0
>>
Rule 909 (If a string is "ii->i" and tensor number of dimensions is equal to 3, the shape has to be a power of 2.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (v_2 = "ii->i") ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 3) then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : ∃p ∈ [0, 10] : shape(v_1, i) = 2*p
>>
Rule 910 (if the string is constant and number of dimensions equals to one or the number of dimension is zero, then type should not be boolean)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if v_2 = "constant" ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 1) then dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0
>>
Rule 911 (if tensor data type is string, its content can only equal to “none” or "constant")
{v_1: tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 11 then (v_1 = "none") ∨ (v_1 = "constant")
>>
Rule 912 (if maximum value for a tensor is less than 0 and minimum is greater than -100 and ndim bigger than 1, then type for that tensor should be float or complex)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (max(v_1) < 0) ∧ (min(v_1) > -100) ∧ (ndim(v_1) > 1) then (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10)
>>
Rule 913 (if shape of the tensor in 0 dimension is less than 5 and more than one dimensions are there, string cant be equal to 'constant')
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (shape(v_1, 0) < 5) ∧ (ndim(v_1) > 1) then v_2 ≠ "constant"
>>
Rule 914 (If tensor v_1 has a more than 1 dimension, and if its first element value is greater than 100 or smaller than -100 and its a flat or int type tensor then its shape should not be equal )
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (v_1 > 100 ∨ v_1 < -100) ∧ ((6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∨ (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5)) then ∀i ∈ [1, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, 0) ≠ shape(v_1, i)
>>
Rule 915 (If dtype is a complex type, then the string must be 'none')
{v_1: tensor, v_2 : str} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10) then v_2 = "none"
>>
Rule 916 (if tensor v_1 number of dimensions is equal to 3, the result of the sum between dimension 0 and dimension 1 has to smaller than dimension 2 or the string equal constant)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 3) then (shape(v_1, 0) + shape(v_1, 1) < shape(v_1, 2)) ∨ (v_2 = "constant")
>>
Rule 917 (if tensor v_1 has more than 1 dimension and v_2 string does not equals "none", the shapes of v_1 should not be zero, or all its element should be smaller than its max element.)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (v_2 ≠ "none") then ((∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≠ 0)) ∨ ((∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : v_1 < max(v_1)))
>>
Rule 918 (if data type is bool and there are at least two dimensions all values on the tensor have to be equals to each other)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 0) ∧ (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2) then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : (v_1 = min(v_1))
>>
Rule 919 (if dtype of tensor equals string and shape is bigger than 1000, then the string must be 'none')
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 11) ∧ (shape(v_1, 0) > 1000) then v_2 = "none"
>>
Rule 920 (If the tensor's number of dimension is equal to 1 or 0, and its data type is not bool, its max value can't be more than 10000.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_1) = 1) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) ≠ 0) then max(v_1) ≤ 10000
>>
Rule 921 (If the input tensor v_1 is 3-dimensional and if max(v_1) equals to 0, at least one of the shape values should be more than 10, and the String value must not be sum)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 3) ∧ (max(v_1) = 0) then (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 10) ∧ (v_2 ≠ "sum")
>>
Rule 922 (if the tensor data type is integer and its number of dimension equal to 3, it must have shape value is greater than 2 in at least one dimension or string must equal none)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 3) then (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 2) ∨ (v_2 = "none")
>>
Rule 923 (If string type equals "...ij->...ji", then the max of the tensor should be smaller than the multiplication of the shape on dimension 0 by 2)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (v_2 = "...ij->...ji") then max(v_1) < shape(v_1, 0) * 2
>>
Rule 924 (if data type equals boolean, and tensor has exactly one dimension, it must have values of both True and False)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 0) ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 1) then ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : v_1 = true ∧ ∃i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : v_1 = false
>>
Rule 925 (If data type is string then if you multiply shape of zero dimension to minimum values, the result must be less than the shape of 1 if it exists)
{v_1: tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 11 then (shape(v_1, 0) * min(v_1)) < shape(v_1, 1)
>>
Rule 926 ( if the first shape dimension is larger than the second, if number of dimensions is equal to 2, and if the string value equals "tanh" then the max and min value have different sings)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if (shape(v_1, 0) > shape(v_1, 1)) ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∧ (v_2 = "tanh") then (max(v_1) > 0) ∧ (min(v_1) < 0)
>>
Rule 927 (If input tensor v_1 has more than 2 dimensions, and if v_2 string equals to mean, its max * min value must be smaller or equal to 0)
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 ∧ v_2 = "mean" then max(v_1) * min(v_1) ≤ 0
>>
Rule 928 (If a tensor has at least 2 dimensions and data type is float, then the ratio of the largest shape to the smallest shape should be less than 100)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) ≥ 2) ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then (∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: max(v_1) / shape(v_1, i) < 100) ∧ (∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1]: shape(v_1, j)/min(v_1) < 100)
>>
Rule 929 (If the input tensor has one dimension and it's of string type all strings have to be different than each other )
{v_1: tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 ∧ 11 = dtype_(v_1) then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [i+1, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : v_1 ≠ v_1
>>
Rule 930 (If a float tensor has more than 1 dimensions, then minimum * maximum values should be smaller than -1 or string equals to none)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) then (min(v_1) * max(v_1)) < -1 ∨ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1)-1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0)
>>
Rule 931 (If max of input has to smaller than 10 and its number of dimension at least 1 or dtype is a boolean data type and its shape on dim 0 must be more or equal to min of shape)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) > 1) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 0) then max(v_1) ≤ 10 ∧ (shape(v_1, 0) ≥ min(v_1))
>>
Rule 932 (If the shape in at least one dimension of a tensor with at least 1 dimension is same as maximum value, then, it must be a 1 dimensional tensor and the type must be either integer of float.)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) >= 1) ∧ (∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = max(v_1)) then (ndim(v_1) = 1) ∧ ((1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) ∨ (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8))
>>
Rule 933 (if the number of dimensions of the tensor v_1 is exactly 2 or data type is bool then all elements within the tensor must be less than 10)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 2) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 0) then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : ∀j ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 1) - 1] : v_1 < 10
>>
Rule 934 (If data type is float and input tensor ndim = 1, for each number inside this tensor must be greater than its max value divided by 2, else shape should be less than 10 in all dimensions)
{v_1: tensor} |= if (6 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∧ (ndim(v_1) = 1) then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : v_1 > (max(v_1) / 2) ∨ ∀j ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, j) < 10
>>
Rule 935 (If the shape of a tensor has a non-positive value, its data type cannot be float64)
{v_1: tensor} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≤ 0 then dtype_(v_1) ≠ 8
>>
Rule 936 (If tensor data type is string then one of following should be valid: The tensor should be exactly a sequence that represents a valid einsum string, the string variable should match tensor, or string variable is "none")
{v_1: tensor, v_2: str} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 11 then (v_1 = "ii" ∨ v_1 = "ii->i" ∨ v_1 = "i,j->ij" ∨ v_1 = "bij,bjk->bik" ∨ v_1 = "...ij->...ji" ∨ v_1 = "bn,anm,bm->ba" ∨ v_1 = v_2 ∨ v_2 = "none" ∨ v_2 = "mean" ∨ v_2 = "sum" ∨ v_2 = "max" ∨ v_2 = "constant" ∨ v_2 = "tanh")
>>
Rule 937 (If the first parameter is "max", the second parameter must be a tensor whose elements are all non-negative)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = "max" then min(v_2) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 938 (If reduction is none, then keep_dims must be false.)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : bool} |= if v_1 = "none" then v_2 = false
>>
Rule 939 (If the first tensor is 2D, the second tensor must have the same number of columns)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 2 then shape(v_1, 1) = shape(v_2, 0)
>>
Rule 940 (If the first parameter is "tanh", then the second tensor's dtype must be float32 or float64)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = "tanh" then dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8
>>
Rule 941 (If the first tensor has more than 2 dimensions, then the second integer must be greater than zero)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) > 2 then v_2 > 0
>>
Rule 942 (If the first parameter is a tensor and the second parameter is an integer, then the integer must be less than the number of dimensions of the tensor)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= v_2 < ndim(v_1)
>>
Rule 943 (If the first tensor's dtype is int, the second parameter must be an integer within the range of that dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 1 then -128 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ 127 else if dtype_(v_1) = 2 then -32768 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ 32767 else if dtype_(v_1) = 3 then -2147483648 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ 2147483647 else if dtype_(v_1) = 4 then -9223372036854775808 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ 9223372036854775807
>>
Rule 944 (If the first tensor's number of dimensions is greater than one, then the second tensor's shape must match the first tensor's shape except for the first dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) > 1 then ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [1, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 945 (If the first tensor is empty, then the second tensor must also be empty)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = 0 then ∃i ∈ [0, ndim(v_2) - 1] : shape(v_2, i) = 0
>>
Rule 946 (If the first tensor's dtype is boolean, then all elements in the tensor must be either true or false)
{v_1 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 0 then ∀i ∈ [0, shape(v_1, 0) - 1] : v_1[i] = true ∨ v_1[i] = false
>>
Rule 947 (If the first parameter is a string, and it's equal to "mean", the second parameter tensor must have a floating point or complex dtype.)
{v_1 : str, v_2 : tensor} |= if v_1 = "mean" then dtype_(v_2) = 6 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 7 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 8 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10
>>
Rule 948 (If the first tensor's number of dimensions is one, then the second parameter integer must be between 0 and shape(v_1, 0) - 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if ndim(v_1) = 1 then 0 ≤ v_2 ∧ v_2 ≤ shape(v_1, 0) - 1
>>
Rule 949 (If the first parameter's shape at dimension 0 is greater than 10, then the second parameter, an integer, must be less than 100)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= if shape(v_1, 0) > 10 then v_2 < 100
>>
Rule 950 (If the first tensor is a complex type, the second tensor also needs to be a complex type.)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if dtype_(v_1) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 10 then dtype_(v_2) = 9 ∨ dtype_(v_2) = 10
